SUMMARY:Institute of Criminology Big Ideas Lecture - Professor Angie Hobbs 
 'Flourishing\, character and justice: why Plato matters now'
LOCATION:Institute of Criminology\, Sidgwick Site\, Cambridge CB3 9DA and o
 nline
URL:https://talks.cam.ac.uk/talk/index/273143/
CATEGORIES:Rights & Justice,Criminology
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Professor Angie Hobbs\, University of Sheffield\nInsti
 tute of Criminology\nTopics: Rights & Justice\, Criminology\nDetails: http
 s://talks.cam.ac.uk/talk/index/273143/\nSign-up needed\nThis event is part
  of the Institute of Criminology's Public Guest Seminar Series for Michael
 mas Term 2026. A drinks reception follows the talk. These events are free 
 and everyone is welcome. Please register to attend either in-person or onl
 ine by clicking the link at the bottom of this page. \n About What might i
 t mean to live a flourishing life? And what is the relationship between fl
 ourishing and the virtues\, especially justice? In this talk based on her 
 recent book\, Professor Angie Hobbs explores how Plato can help us with th
 ese urgent questions\, and how he addresses the key issue of character for
 mation\, and why it never benefits us to return wrong for wrong. She shows
  how she has used his methodology\, ideas and arguments in a variety of se
 ctors to address contemporary issues in education\, faith–secular debate
 \, health care and the civil service\, and invites the audience to discuss
  with
END:VEVENT
