SUMMARY:LCIL lunchtime conversation: 'What is Special about the Special Tri
 bunal for the Crime of Aggression against Ukraine?'
LOCATION:Lauterpacht Centre for International Law
URL:https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/press/events/2026/12/lunchtime-conversation-w
 hat-special-about-special-tribunal-crime-aggression-against-ukraine
CATEGORIES:Law,International,Criminology
DESCRIPTION:Faculty of Law\nTopics: Law\, International\, Criminology\nDeta
 ils: https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/press/events/2026/12/lunchtime-conversation
 -what-special-about-special-tribunal-crime-aggression-against-ukraine\nSig
 n-up only to join online: https://cam-ac-uk.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_63
 c_m3-CQVuG0bm6uCOPfw\nDate/time: \n\n Friday 4 December 2026 \n\n 1:00pm t
 o 2:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n Lauterpacht Centre for International Law\n\n B
 erkowitz/Finley Lecture Hall\n\n About \n\n Register here if attending onl
 ine   At a time when some international courts and tribunals are under at
 tack\, defunded or otherwise obstructed\, a new one is being created: the 
 Special Tribunal for the Crime of Aggression against Ukraine. Ukrainian le
 gal scholar Dr Gaiane Nuridzhanian \, in conversation with LCIL Fellow Pro
 fessor Sarah Nouwen\, will explore what is special about the tribunal: why
  is it needed\, what is its legal nature\, what are its prospects and the 
 role in the development of international law? \n There is a sandwich lunc
 h at 12.30 pm in the Old Library at the Centre. All lecture attendees welc
 ome.\n The Friday Lunchtime Lecture series is kindly supported by Cambridg
 e University Press & Assessment .
